  "insights": [
    "AI Voice Agent adoption is 30.3% of accounts; 3,486 customers (70%) have not adopted. Starter is the weakest plan at 27.8%. RECOMMENDATION: target in-app onboarding at non-adopters, starting with Starter.",
    "Treatment lifted AI adoption from 27.3% to 33.3% (+22.0% relative, p=4e-06, 95% CI +3.5 to +8.5 pp). 8-week retention moved +1.6 pp (95% CI -1.1 to +4.3), not a significant change. Segment reads are exploratory; the effect is inconclusive in Enterprise (n=534, CI -9.6 to +6.0 pp). RECOMMENDATION: ramp exposure in stages, keep retention as a guardrail, and size a follow-up test for under-powered segments before a full rollout.",
    "AI-handled calls resolve at 82.9% vs 73.6% for human-handled calls, with quality 4.53/5 vs 4.10/5 (observational; AI calls are not randomly assigned). RECOMMENDATION: segment escalations by call type before expanding AI coverage.",
    "The churn model (holdout AUC 0.93) ranks 'Active in last 2 weeks' as the strongest signal (odds ratio 0.24 per SD). 1,757 accounts (35%) sit in the Critical / At risk health bands, carrying $7,072,139 in ARR. RECOMMENDATION: route them to customer success, prioritised by churn risk x ARR."
